          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Driveway resurfacing cost</strong> runs $3-7 per square foot for asphalt and $4-10 for concrete, which puts a typical two-car driveway at roughly $1,800-6,000 — 40-60% below replacement. That savings is real only when the base underneath is sound.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you spend anything, look for <strong class="text-white">alligator cracking, settlement, or standing water</strong>. Any of those means the base has failed and an overlay will crack through within two seasons. Where the base is solid, insist on <strong class="text-white">a specified compacted thickness</strong> and itemized prep work, and get three quotes from established local contractors.
          </p>
